text We wait by the edge of the gym for the curtain to rise on the recital.
text @[Tomoya]
text Ready, Nagisa...?
text @[Tomoya]
text Don't let yourself get distracted. Just think about the play.
text @[Tomoya]
text C'mon, it's almost our turn on stage.
text @[Tomoya]
text You're feeling nervous, aren't you? Do you not need to look over your script one last time?
text @[Tomoya]
text C'mon, your script.
text Nagisa shows me the script in her hands as she holds it up to her chest.
text @[Tomoya]
text Let's have a celebration once this is all over.
text @[Tomoya]
text I'd prefer for the celebration to be just us, but...
text @[Tomoya]
text Well, I guess I'll invite Sanae-san, cause she's cute.
text @[Tomoya]
text Oh, fine. I'll invite the old man too.
text @[Tomoya]
text Okay? Let's have a celebration with the four of us.
text @[Tomoya]
text So let's do everything we can right now.
sound L0M.aac
text @[Nagisa]
text Okay...
text Nagisa finally opens her script and begins to look down at it.
text Up on the gymnasium's stage, I can see the curtain as it's quite literally on the verge of rising.
text Spectators have begun to gather.
text I look for the old man and Sanae-san among them.
text They just might show themselves to Nagisa before she starts.
text But I think that any words of encouragement they'd give her would only hurt her more, and I want to keep that from happening right now.
text Their remarks would truly be sincere and kind, but that's what would ultimately hurt her.
text But I don't see them anywhere in the distance.
text @[Tomoya]
text Hey, Nagisa? You just keep reading your script. I'm going to leave for a second.
sound L0N.aac
text @[Nagisa]
text ...
text There's no reply, but she must have heard me.
text I leave Nagisa with Sunohara and head off to find her parents.
